## Independent practice

Complete each item with models + evidence.

1. Practice 1: A cell model shows a membrane separating inside/outside. Explain one job of the membrane and predict what happens if a channel protein for nutrient X stops working. Use numbers only if helpful (relative rates 2:1).
2. Practice 2: A cell model shows a membrane separating inside/outside. Explain one job of the membrane and predict what happens if a channel protein for nutrient X stops working. Use numbers only if helpful (relative rates 3:-1).
3. Practice 3: A cell model shows a membrane separating inside/outside. Explain one job of the membrane and predict what happens if a channel protein for nutrient X stops working. Use numbers only if helpful (relative rates 4:2).
